#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Batch 2: establishing views, second designs. A = wind cave with skylight forests, B = tidal shelf with colour masses and a far goal, C = field of living air sacs at dusk.
R = '/home/user/workspace/r3/prompts'
HEAD = "A wide 16:9 landscape frame from a big-budget natural-history film about an alien world. It must read as real {night}location photography, not artwork: {cam}, true lens perspective, fine physical surface detail{where}, {haze}, {grain}."
TAIL = "It must feel like a place you could walk into: firm ground in the foreground, a readable route into the middle distance, far landmarks dissolving in the air. Nothing posed, nothing glowing unless it is lit, no painterly brushwork, no illustration styling. No people, no buildings, no cameras, drones or equipment, no text, no watermark, no border."
A = [HEAD.format(night='', cam='24 mm lens, deep focus, natural light only', where='', haze='humid haze building with distance', grain='slight film grain'),
"""THE PLACE. The inside of the windpipe of a creature the size of a mountain range that died ages ago. It is now a tunnel-cave about two hundred metres high and wide that runs straight into the distance. Its walls and roof are built from regular hoops of pale cartilage, each hoop as thick as a house, with dark wet rock between them, so the whole tunnel is ribbed, ring after ring, like the inside of a hose. Along its length the roof has fallen in at intervals, leaving ragged skylights. Through each skylight the sun comes down in one thick shaft through the wet air, and under each shaft a whole island of rainforest has grown on the rubble: tree ferns, broad-leaved giants, hanging vines, moss over the broken hoops. Thin waterfalls drop through the skylights. A river runs along the tunnel floor between the islands. The tunnel breathes: a slow tongue of cloud slides along under the roof toward the viewer and curls around the skylights.""",
"""VIEWPOINT AND LAYOUT, asymmetric, nothing centred. Seen from standing height on mossy rubble at the river's edge, in the dark stretch of tunnel before the first skylight. The river runs from the bottom left corner away down the tunnel: the obvious route into the picture. Close on the right, in shade, a fallen hoop segment covered in moss carries a cluster of pale translucent bladder-like growths, each the size of a person, a few of them puffing out fine golden dust. In the middle distance the first forest island stands in its shaft of sun, right of centre, its trees tiny under the roof, a flock of small winged animals circling up the shaft. Far beyond it, much smaller and paler in the haze, a second shaft of light falls on a second island, and beyond that a third is barely visible. The ribbed walls curve up on both sides and are lost in darkness and cloud overhead.""",
"""LIGHT AND WEATHER. The only light is daylight from the skylights: hard warm sun in the shafts, soft green bounce light near them, deep cool darkness between, wet highlights on rock and leaves, mist in every beam. Colours: deep green, wet black rock, pale bone, small amounts of gold. The mood is vast, beautiful and lethal."""]
B = [HEAD.format(night='', cam='24 mm lens, deep focus, natural light only', where='', haze='sea haze building with distance', grain='slight film grain'),
"""THE PLACE. A tidal shelf on a cold coast at low tide, soon after sunrise, sea fog burning off. The shelf is the exposed lung of a creature the size of a mountain range that died ages ago: bone-white, porous and honeycombed like weathered coral limestone, tide-stained and streaked with droppings. It is completely overgrown with animal life, not plants: wide carpets of crimson feathery gill-plumes like the crowns of giant tube worms, beds of pale barnacle-like cones, black-green ribbon weed, orange crusts. Set into the shelf are the open ends of the airways: enormous round throats twenty to sixty metres across, each a low broken collar of ivory cartilage built from stacked rings, like the cut end of a giant ribbed hose, none taller than a house, all tilted at slightly different angles. Every throat is exhaling at the same moment: a dense column of cold white vapour pours up from each and leans the same way on the wind.""",
"""VIEWPOINT AND LAYOUT, asymmetric, nothing centred. Seen from standing height at the edge of a tide channel. The channel of pale teal seawater runs from the bottom centre away across the shelf, bending between the throats toward the far distance: the obvious route into the picture. On the right, about forty metres away, the nearest throat: its wet ringed rim, the dark opening, crimson plumes crowding the rim and bending outward in the rush of air. On the left bank in the foreground the crimson plume carpet comes right up to the viewer's feet, wet and glistening. More than twenty other exhaling throats stand at every distance along the channel, shrinking and paling into the fog. In the middle distance four tall pale animals on very long thin stilt legs wade the channel in a line, small beside the throats; a flock of hundreds of small dark flyers wheels through one distant column. At the far end of the channel, huge and faint in the fog, the broken end of the main windpipe lies against a headland like a ringed tunnel mouth hundreds of metres high, breathing out the fog bank itself.""",
"""LIGHT AND WEATHER. A low sun, back left, just breaking through the fog: warm pale-gold light edges every vapour column and lays long reflections on the wet shelf; shadows stay cold blue-grey. Colours: arterial crimson in broad masses, ivory bone, pale teal water, wet black, small patches of orange. The mood is cold, quiet and lethal."""]
C = [HEAD.format(night='night-time ', cam='fast 24 mm lens at high sensitivity, available light only', where=' where light reaches it', haze='mist thickening with distance', grain='visible sensor noise in the shadows'),
"""THE PLACE. Deep dusk in a shallow valley on the body of a creature the size of a mountain range that died ages ago. Its lung has weathered open here, and the valley floor is crowded with its air sacs, still alive: thousands of rounded membrane domes packed together in clusters like frogspawn, from the size of a car to the size of a house, a few much larger. Their skins are thin, leathery and wet, veined like a leaf or a bat's wing, pale where stretched and dark where slack. They breathe: at this moment some are swollen tight and others have sagged and wrinkled. Colonies of luminous organisms live inside them, so each sac glows faintly from within, cold blue-green with a dim amber core, unevenly, showing the veins and the dark shapes of things caught inside. The sacs exhale a low mist through puckered pores; it lies knee-deep over the ground, catches their light and drains slowly downhill.""",
"""VIEWPOINT AND LAYOUT, asymmetric, nothing centred. Seen from standing height on a wet black rock path. The path runs from the bottom right away down the valley between the clusters, beside a narrow black stream that mirrors the glow: the obvious route into the picture. Close on the left, one house-sized sac fills the left edge of the frame, near enough to see its veins, beads of moisture and the silhouette of a winged animal trapped inside against the light. The clusters recede down the valley at every distance, dimmer and bluer in the mist, hundreds of soft lights. Small pale moth-like animals spiral toward several of them. On the far side the valley ends at a dark cliff where one colossal ringed windpipe opening stands black against the sky. The sky is the last band of deep blue and dull orange twilight low on the horizon, with the first stars above.""",
"""LIGHT AND EXPOSURE. Exposed for the living light, so most of the frame is dark: blue-black land, soft cyan-green pools of light on mist and wet rock around each sac, a few amber points. The glow is weak, falls off quickly and is never even. The mood is silent, beautiful and lethal."""]
for k, parts in {'A-est-v2': A, 'B-est-v2': B, 'C-est-v2': C}.items():
    open(f'{R}/{k}.txt', 'w').write('\n\n'.join(parts) + '\n\n' + TAIL + '\n'); print(k, sum(map(len, parts)))
